# HELLO/WORLD — Environment Variables

Copy this file to `.env` and fill in the values before deploying.

## Local development

```env
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://customer_db_owner_user:TSZsw8x2YpeNfFo9TefRErxZXsh1FlmQz4aRN6BuSruaq7VnQpLuX144bQsD8f6F@db-r5710-269-47.db.hostoflow.app:5432/customer_db
PORT=3000
NODE_ENV=development
```

## HostOflow platform deployment

When you link the database service on the platform, the following env vars are injected automatically:

```
DB_db_r5710_269_47_HOST=db-r5710-269-47.tenant-hywang-lab
DB_db_r5710_269_47_PORT=5432
DB_db_r5710_269_47_NAME=customer_db
DB_db_r5710_269_47_USERNAME=customer_db_owner_user
DB_db_r5710_269_47_PASSWORD=TSZsw8x2YpeNfFo9TefRErxZXsh1FlmQz4aRN6BuSruaq7VnQpLuX144bQsD8f6F
PORT=3000
NODE_ENV=production
```

> The app auto-detects these variables — no manual configuration needed after linking the service.

## Notes

- `DATABASE_URL` takes priority over individual `DB_*` vars.
- The PostgreSQL schema (`greetings` table) is created automatically on first startup.
- For local testing, make sure the database has **Public Access** enabled in the HostOflow platform.
